    {
      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "When an option that is NOT declared as a count is repeated with numeric values and one of those values is 1, the parser silently adds them up instead of collecting them: parser(\"-x 3 -x 1\") returns { x: 4 } while parser(\"-x 3 -x 2\") correctly returns { x: [3, 2] }. Repeated values must always be collected into an array (\"-x 3 -x 1\" gives [3, 1], \"-x 1 -x 1\" gives [1, 1], \"-x 1 -x 3\" gives [1, 3]) whatever the numbers, and options that ARE declared under count must keep incrementing exactly as before (\"-v -v -v\" with count: [\"v\"] gives 3). Nothing else about duplicate-argument handling may change. Source is lib/yargs-parser.ts; tests are compiled with npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json and run with npm test (mocha); test/yargs-parser.mjs imports the built library.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
